  </requires>

  <description>
    <p>
      Diapason is a music player that brings together the libraries on your Jellyfin, Plex, Subsonic/Navidrome and MPD servers, as well as the music stored on your computer. It started as a fork of Finamp and grew into a multi-backend player.
    </p>
    <p>What Diapason can do:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Stream from Jellyfin, Plex, Subsonic/Navidrome, MPD and local folders</li>
      <li>Download tracks for offline listening, with optional transcoding</li>
      <li>Control desktop playback from other devices with Diapason Connect and local network discovery</li>
      <li>Build smart playlists from rules on genre, BPM, rating, format and more</li>
      <li>Follow time-synced lyrics, with LRCLIB as a fallback</li>
      <li>Enjoy a spectrum visualizer and a full-screen player</li>
      <li>Scrobble to Last.fm and ListenBrainz</li>
      <li>Use your media keys and desktop media controls through MPRIS</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">fr.nytuo.diapason.desktop</launchable>

